1
00:01:33,799 --> 00:01:36,040
Writer Fang Haowen's recent actions have drawn attention.

2
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:36,840
Experts advise

3
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,480
that the possibility of depression

4
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,799
or other mental distress cannot be ruled out.

5
00:01:39,799 --> 00:01:41,560
They urge the public to be objective

6
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,640
and avoid stigmatization.

7
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:43,640
How is this depression?

8
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,760
Isn't he just crazy?

9
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:45,760
This is definitely not depression.

10
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:46,680
This is Bipolar disorder.

11
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,239
With depression, you hurt yourself first.

12
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,400
With Bipolar disorder, you hurt others, then yourself.

13
00:01:50,599 --> 00:01:51,920
He might even end up killing himself.

14
00:01:52,519 --> 00:01:53,760
I think you have a touch of Bipolar disorder.

15
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:55,719
Since when do I have Bipolar disorder?

16
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Don't you have Bipolar disorder?

17
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:57,799
Don't make a scene here.

18
00:01:57,799 --> 00:01:58,280
If we start fighting here,

19
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,239
neither of us will look good.

20
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:00,920
Then let's fight! Come on, hit me!

21
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:04,439
I'm sorry, I'm sorry! I'm sorry, honey!

22
00:02:04,439 --> 00:02:05,799
My hair! My hair is gone!

23
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,159
Pick it up.

24
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,120
Mr. He... Mr. He! Mr. He!

25
00:02:11,439 --> 00:02:13,439
Where can I find Mr. Fang?

26
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,520
I have a few questions for him.

27
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:35,400
The Wicked Outsider

28
00:02:54,759 --> 00:02:56,840
A Final Letter to the World

29
00:02:56,879 --> 00:02:58,080
Fang Haowen

30
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:00,280
A.k.a. The Solitary Chanter

31
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:03,240
This letter is what I leave to this world,

32
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:04,599
my final voice.

33
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,520
By the time you read these words,

34
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,439
I will have shed this mortal shell.

35
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:10,560
I've read the classics since childhood,

36
00:03:10,759 --> 00:03:12,960
shouldering the mission to awaken the world.

37
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:15,400
Unappreciated and misunderstood.

38
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,759
After I'm gone,

39
00:03:17,039 --> 00:03:17,879
my words

40
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,319
will one day be recognized by the world.

41
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,319
Then,

42
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,120
they will regret

43
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:26,479
their indifference and injustice toward me today.

44
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:32,520
Mr. He! Mr. He! It's Bie Fan!

45
00:03:32,759 --> 00:03:33,520
Speak Mandarin!

46
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,360
I... It's Bie Fan.

47
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,879
You again?

48
00:03:36,879 --> 00:03:38,280
Mr. Fang is trying to kill himself again!

49
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:40,400
He died again?

50
00:03:40,719 --> 00:03:41,520
Are you sure?

51
00:03:42,199 --> 00:03:42,800
I'm not sure.

52
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:43,800
If you're not sure, what the hell are you talking about?

53
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,319
But I saw his suicide note!

54
00:03:45,639 --> 00:03:47,560
He wants to bury himself in his hometown!

55
00:03:47,919 --> 00:03:50,479
Hachun City, Xing County, Fangjiatun, Yaolong Ridge.

56
00:03:50,479 --> 00:03:51,800
The fifth mountain on the left,

57
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:52,919
halfway up, next to a tree.

58
00:03:53,759 --> 00:03:55,199
Kid, listen to me.

59
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,759
Go to his hometown right now.

60
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,479
And then?

61
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,039
And then,

62
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,560
once you make sure he's dead,

63
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:08,199
call me to let me know, okay?

64
00:04:09,479 --> 00:04:10,039
Okay.

65
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:28,879
Hey, Sihai.

66
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,160
Hey, Bie Fan.

67
00:04:30,399 --> 00:04:31,399
Where are you?

68
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:33,720
I'm at the train station.

69
00:04:34,839 --> 00:04:35,759
I'm at the train station too.

70
00:04:35,839 --> 00:04:37,000
Where in the station?

71
00:04:37,399 --> 00:04:39,000
At the ticket gate for Hachun.

72
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:40,480
Aren't we going back to Liaocheng?

73
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,240
Why are you over there?

74
00:04:41,399 --> 00:04:42,839
Wait for me, I'll be right there.

75
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:46,319
Train 31 to Hachun

76
00:04:46,439 --> 00:04:48,279
is now boarding.

77
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,680
Please hurry and line up to board.

78
00:04:55,959 --> 00:04:57,279
Bie Fan! Bie Fan!

79
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:58,560
Where are you going?

80
00:05:00,519 --> 00:05:01,920
Mr. Fang is going to kill himself.

81
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:03,439
I have to go and save him.

82
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,079
He's a total fraud.

83
00:05:05,079 --> 00:05:06,560
You can't believe what he says anymore.

84
00:05:06,839 --> 00:05:08,000
I read his suicide note.

85
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,279
It's definitely real.

86
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,920
But what if he really wants to kill himself?

87
00:05:12,079 --> 00:05:13,680
What if he's really sick?

88
00:05:14,199 --> 00:05:15,680
I'll just go check on him and come back.

89
00:05:16,319 --> 00:05:17,040
Well, fine.

90
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:18,360
Then... then stay safe.

91
00:05:18,879 --> 00:05:20,360
Here, take this to eat on the way.

92
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,319
Then... then stay safe.

93
00:05:23,319 --> 00:05:24,480
Don't believe everything he says!

94
00:05:24,879 --> 00:05:25,839
You hear me?

95
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,279
I hear you.

96
00:05:28,759 --> 00:05:30,439
Bie Fan believes everything.

97
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,079
Is this you?

98
00:05:34,839 --> 00:05:36,680
This is my best friend.

99
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,160
This young guy looks pretty sharp.

100
00:05:39,759 --> 00:05:40,639
What did you buy?

101
00:05:40,839 --> 00:05:41,680
Stinky tofu.

102
00:05:54,279 --> 00:05:56,759
To the left of Yaolong Ridge,

103
00:05:57,560 --> 00:06:01,480
halfway up the fifth mountain.

104
00:06:04,639 --> 00:06:06,399
Where do we start counting from?

105
00:06:15,879 --> 00:06:17,480
You fake-peddling crooks!

106
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,439
You'd even scam the dead!

107
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,040
I just got these glasses.

108
00:06:57,319 --> 00:06:58,199
Who is it?

109
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,040
You scared me!

110
00:07:13,439 --> 00:07:14,399
Oh my God!

111
00:07:15,959 --> 00:07:17,319
Mr. Fang!

112
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,720
Mr. Fang!

113
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,480
You can't die!

114
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:24,680
Mr. Fang!

115
00:07:27,639 --> 00:07:29,240
Mr. Fang! You can't die!

116
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:30,560
Mr. Fang!

117
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:32,240
I won't let you die!

118
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,040
You're choking me!

119
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:34,959
Let go!

120
00:07:36,199 --> 00:07:37,399
Mr. Fang, come down!

121
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,360
Mr. Fang, you can't die!

122
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,480
Mr. Fang!

123
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,879
Mr. Fang! Fang!

124
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,519
Oh my God!

125
00:07:51,199 --> 00:07:52,319
Mr. Fang!

126
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,079
You're okay now.

127
00:07:54,079 --> 00:07:55,240
You're not going to die.

128
00:07:55,519 --> 00:07:56,519
Why is it...

129
00:07:58,279 --> 00:07:59,319
Why is it you again?!

130
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:00,319
Your mom...

131
00:08:00,319 --> 00:08:01,800
My mom passed away.

132
00:08:02,319 --> 00:08:02,600
You...

133
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:03,560
I'm fine.

134
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:06,160
My mom went to be with my dad.

135
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:06,800
It's just that...

136
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,600
Are you crazy?!

137
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,519
Aren't you the sick one?

138
00:08:09,519 --> 00:08:11,240
What the hell do you want?!

139
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,680
I don't want you to die.

140
00:08:14,319 --> 00:08:15,160
I want to die!

141
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,920
I can't let you die!

142
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:17,759
I want to die!

143
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,399
I just can't let you die!

144
00:08:19,399 --> 00:08:20,920
I want to die! I want to die! I want to die!

145
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:21,680
I want to die!

146
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,639
No!

147
00:08:30,879 --> 00:08:31,439
Get lost!

148
00:08:42,519 --> 00:08:43,159
Let go!

149
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,519
Let... let go!

150
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:53,240
Let go!

151
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,200
I want to die!

152
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,919
What's it to you if I want to die?

153
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:01,799
I...

154
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,080
I want to die!

155
00:09:03,399 --> 00:09:04,320
I want to die!

156
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:06,919
Mr. Fang, your condition is getting worse again.

157
00:09:06,919 --> 00:09:09,360
Get lost! Get lost!

158
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,440
You kicked my tombstone!

159
00:09:32,159 --> 00:09:33,639
My Nothingness... how did my Nothingness disappear?

160
00:09:33,919 --> 00:09:34,559
Where is the Nothingness?

161
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:37,159
Where is my Nothingness?

162
00:09:37,279 --> 00:09:38,240
Is this it?

163
00:09:42,639 --> 00:09:43,519
Come on, give me the Nothingness.

164
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,399
I'll give it to you if you don't kill yourself.

165
00:09:47,159 --> 00:09:48,120
Give me the Nothingness!

166
00:09:53,279 --> 00:09:53,879
Fine, I won't kill myself.

167
00:09:53,879 --> 00:09:54,960
Come on, give me the Nothingness.

168
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,200
You... you've lied to me.

169
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,159
I don't believe you.

170
00:10:00,159 --> 00:10:00,720
You even...

171
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:01,679
You...

172
00:10:04,679 --> 00:10:06,440
Came, loved...

173
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,120
Plagiarized!

174
00:10:13,159 --> 00:10:14,759
How can I die without my Nothingness?

175
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:15,879
Stop right there!

176
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:05,120
Stop! Give Nothingness back to me!

177
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:09,799
Stop! Give Nothingness back to me!

178
00:11:11,519 --> 00:11:12,799
Oh my God!

179
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,720
Nothingness!

180
00:11:18,559 --> 00:11:20,039
The flowers hadn't bloomed last time I was here.

181
00:11:21,679 --> 00:11:22,960
Good thing it wasn't hot.

182
00:11:23,399 --> 00:11:24,639
Or I would've been burned.

183
00:11:25,519 --> 00:11:26,279
What are you doing?!

184
00:11:26,279 --> 00:11:27,480
Seriously. Oh my god!

185
00:11:28,799 --> 00:11:30,600
But this is spicy!

186
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:31,960
Where are the tissues?

187
00:11:32,039 --> 00:11:33,039
Quick, wipe it off! Wipe it off!

188
00:12:06,679 --> 00:12:07,440
Bie Fan

189
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,840
Bie Fan, come out!

190
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,399
I won't hit you anymore, Bie Fan.

191
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,240
Bie Fan!

192
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:15,360
Bie Fan!

193
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:16,399
Bie Fan!

194
00:12:21,519 --> 00:12:23,480
Um, you two look at each other.

195
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:24,639
Kiss! Kiss!

196
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:26,720
Honey.

197
00:12:27,039 --> 00:12:28,720
These canola flowers are really

198
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:32,600
beautiful!

199
00:12:39,279 --> 00:12:40,080
Stop!

200
00:12:41,759 --> 00:12:42,320
You think I won't

201
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:44,440
run right over your body?

202
00:12:46,399 --> 00:12:48,039
Wedding photos, Honey.

203
00:12:54,559 --> 00:12:55,240
Bee!

204
00:12:56,799 --> 00:12:57,480
Bee!

205
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:58,960
There's a bee!

206
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:00,440
There's a bee!

207
00:13:06,399 --> 00:13:07,120
Mr. Fang!

208
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:09,600
There's a bee! There's a bee, Mr. Fang!

209
00:13:19,759 --> 00:13:20,519
There are bees.

210
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,039
There are bees.

211
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:23,519
There are bees.

212
00:13:23,519 --> 00:13:24,600
If you didn't want us having hot pot, just say so!

213
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:25,279
Run!

214
00:13:25,399 --> 00:13:26,159
There are bees!

215
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:26,799
Oh my God!

216
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:28,559
There are bees!

217
00:13:28,559 --> 00:13:29,639
Bees! There are bees!

218
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:37,279
Why is this happening?

219
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,919
Are they only stinging me?

220
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:43,759
Are you guys crazy?

221
00:13:44,159 --> 00:13:45,960
What's going on? Why are you running?

222
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:47,279
My face is burning!

223
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:49,240
I'm getting disfigured here!

224
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:52,200
He stole from me!

225
00:13:52,559 --> 00:13:54,120
What did he steal?

226
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:54,879
He stole my "mei"—my Nothingness!

227
00:13:54,879 --> 00:13:56,000
How many tons of coal did he steal?

228
00:13:56,799 --> 00:13:57,759
Not coal!

229
00:13:58,159 --> 00:13:58,720
The "mei" that means Nothingness!

230
00:13:58,720 --> 00:13:59,879
If you have nothing, what did he steal?

231
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,559
I mean the word Nothingness!

232
00:14:01,559 --> 00:14:02,120
I get it.

233
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,519
This young man must have stolen his money.

234
00:14:03,519 --> 00:14:04,240
So he has no money to buy coal.

235
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:05,120
His pockets are completely empty.

236
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:05,799
What?

237
00:14:06,759 --> 00:14:07,440
What? No!

238
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,240
You're making up a story!

239
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:08,879
No!

240
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:09,759
It's the...

241
00:14:10,639 --> 00:14:13,200
The Nothingness in "The man of old is gone, the waters are cold today"!

242
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,240
He's sick.

243
00:14:18,639 --> 00:14:19,320
Bipolar disorder.

244
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,559
Oh, he's sick just because you say so?

245
00:14:22,519 --> 00:14:24,960
The farce of washed-up author Fang Haowen is escalating.

246
00:14:25,159 --> 00:14:27,519
Experts claim he suffers from a mental illness.

247
00:14:27,679 --> 00:14:29,000
He slapped judge Hei Cong,

248
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,240
author Ren Fangfang,

249
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,120
and even made a huge scene at a campus cafeteria,

250
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,799
holding filth to pollute the future of our nation.

251
00:14:36,399 --> 00:14:38,000
Even if he's cured, he'll still be drooling.

252
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Give me my Nothingness! Give it back!

253
00:14:39,759 --> 00:14:41,000
He definitely has a serious illness, Honey.

254
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:41,799
Stay away from him!

255
00:14:41,799 --> 00:14:42,559
Don't catch whatever he has!

256
00:14:42,559 --> 00:14:43,200
It's fine. It's nothing.

257
00:14:44,159 --> 00:14:45,440
Forget it. Just give it back.

258
00:14:48,519 --> 00:14:49,120
I understand.

259
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:50,320
Even though we got dirty,

260
00:14:50,399 --> 00:14:51,440
he is a sick man.

261
00:14:52,799 --> 00:14:53,799
WeChat Pay received 500 yuan.

262
00:14:53,799 --> 00:14:54,480
Thanks.

263
00:14:54,679 --> 00:14:56,360
It's camping. We like it lively anyway.

264
00:14:57,759 --> 00:14:59,000
I don't mind if you scan it or not.

265
00:14:59,000 --> 00:14:59,960
Get that illness treated soon!

266
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,360
We understand!

267
00:15:02,559 --> 00:15:04,279
WeChat Pay received 500 yuan.

268
00:15:04,279 --> 00:15:06,000
WeChat Pay received 500 yuan.

269
00:15:07,679 --> 00:15:08,360
Not enough.

270
00:15:08,679 --> 00:15:09,320
Give me a little more.

271
00:15:11,399 --> 00:15:13,080
WeChat Pay received 1,000 yuan.

272
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,320
Come again when you're free!

273
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:30,759
I need to use the bathroom.

274
00:15:30,759 --> 00:15:31,600
I don't believe you.

275
00:15:33,919 --> 00:15:35,360
I really need to use the bathroom.

276
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:37,320
Mr. Fang, I'm not a kid anymore.

277
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:40,480
Mr. Fang can't hold it anymore.

278
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:43,320
Mr. Fang, just tell me what you're trying to do.

279
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,759
I'm not falling for your tricks this time.

280
00:15:44,759 --> 00:15:46,279
I need to use the bathroom.

281
00:15:46,639 --> 00:15:47,600
The bathroom.

282
00:15:47,919 --> 00:15:49,240
I've said it so many times.

283
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:00,360
Now do you believe me?

284
00:16:20,799 --> 00:16:21,639
What's wrong with him?

285
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:23,440
He's sick.

286
00:16:23,879 --> 00:16:25,200
Pretty seriously, too.

287
00:16:25,279 --> 00:16:26,639
He's completely incontinent.

288
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:30,240
No, he has Bipolar disorder.

289
00:16:32,799 --> 00:16:35,720
Mr. Fang, you don't need to be embarrassed.

290
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,440
Thank you.

291
00:16:41,519 --> 00:16:42,919
No one has ever cared about me before.

292
00:16:44,039 --> 00:16:45,120
That's why I got Bipolar disorder.

293
00:16:47,039 --> 00:16:47,960
Now that I have you,

294
00:16:51,919 --> 00:16:53,080
I feel like I'm cured.

295
00:16:54,519 --> 00:16:55,480
Really?

296
00:16:57,759 --> 00:16:58,720
You're a chef, right?

297
00:16:59,759 --> 00:17:01,039
Yes, Mr. Fang.

298
00:17:01,039 --> 00:17:03,000
I'm a chef.

299
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:06,279
Then what kind of dishes do you usually like to cook?

300
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:10,039
I can cook a lot of dishes.

301
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:13,079
My best dish is Squirrel Fish.

302
00:17:13,079 --> 00:17:14,240
Squirrel Fish?

303
00:17:14,799 --> 00:17:16,559
